{"numberOfHits":1,"results":[{"id":"GO:0044826","isObsolete":false,"name":"viral genome integration into host DNA","definition":{"text":"The insertion into a host genome of viral DNA, usually by the action of an integrase enzyme. Once integrated, the provirus persists in the host cell and serves as a template for the transcription of viral genes and replication of the viral genome, leading to the production of new viruses.","xrefs":[{"dbCode":"PMID","dbId":"19091057"}]},"synonyms":[{"name":"viral genome integration","type":"exact"}],"children":[{"id":"GO:0044823","relation":"part_of"}],"history":[{"timestamp":"2024-09-05","action":"Added","category":"CONSTRAINT","text":"Bad taxon ID"},{"timestamp":"2014-02-06","action":"Added","category":"TERM","text":"viral genome integration into host DNA"},{"timestamp":"2014-02-06","action":"Added","category":"RELATION","text":"has part GO:0075713 (establishment of integrated proviral latency)"},{"timestamp":"2014-02-06","action":"Added","category":"SYNONYM","text":"viral genome integration"},{"timestamp":"2014-02-06","action":"Added","category":"DEFINITION","text":"The insertion into a host genome of viral DNA, usually by the action of an integrase enzyme. Once integrated, the provirus persists in the host cell and serves as a template for the transcription of viral genes and replication of the viral genome, leading to the production of new viruses."},{"timestamp":"2014-02-06","action":"Added","category":"RELATION","text":"has part GO:0039692 (single stranded viral RNA replication via double stranded DNA intermediate)"},{"timestamp":"2014-02-06","action":"Added","category":"RELATION","text":"is a GO:0016032 (viral process)"},{"timestamp":"2014-02-06","action":"Added","category":"RELATION","text":"part of GO:0019058 (viral life cycle)"}],"xRefs":[{"dbCode":"UniProtKB-KW","dbId":"KW-1179","name":"Viral genome integration"}],"taxonConstraints":[{"ancestorId":"GO:0044826","ancestorName":"viral genome integration into host DNA","relationship":"never_in_taxon","taxId":"4896","taxIdType":"NCBITaxon","taxName":"Schizosaccharomyces pombe"}],"aspect":"biological_process","usage":"Unrestricted","goDiscussions":[{"title":"Viral Processes","url":"http://wiki.geneontology.org/index.php/Virus_terms"}]}],"pageInfo":null}